<!--
  RM_TwilightSeaFloorLife.xml          TerminalBiomes · authored 2026-10-03 (belt r37)
  SEA_FISHABLES_ALIVE_IN_DEPTHS_1 — the TWILIGHT SEA portion.

  Owner, at the bench 2026-09-26, typed: "All the fishables should also be
  alive and moving around in the depths (this is true for ALL seas)."
  Ten of the Twilight's twelve catches had no living body. The design is the
  BENCH table in the_twilight_deep_content_2026-09-26.md §5 ("the body specs
  below are those descriptions turned into race fields, not new invention"):
  speed, size, groups, diet and predation are read off it. Every number that
  table does not give (health, hunger, combat power, life expectancy,
  wildness, tool power) is a PROVISIONAL first guess (owner ruling
  2026-10-03), sized against the Grey's RM_GreySeaFloorLife.xml siblings.

  Pairing: the catch items were renamed RM_<X> -> RM_<X>Catch in the same
  change (GREYSEA_CATCH_TIER_RENAME_1's shape), so RM_Niim is now the fish
  and RM_NiimCatch what a shore net brings up.

  Schooling: legal only under the waveglass, i.e. this floor (the_twilight_deep.md
  "the solitary law's boundary"). Niim alone carries herdAnimal, the lit shoal
  of the columns; noolim is the dark shoal of the between (Q3, ruled TWO,
  2026-09-26 card). Pallu and nuudal come in groups without herd behaviour.

  Not built here (the table's own notes, each its own mechanism): the glows
  (niim dot-line, aluun gold, liiru line, hollu faint) -> living-light work;
  pallu spawning only on skylight cells and counting as the skylight price;
  aluun placed per kelp stem; tikkarr climbing oruvell; oobo's drop ambush;
  hollu's contact sting as a hediff. Murrol carries RM_ChannelNativeExtension
  (the channel current's ruled exemption) and kellu butchers to lamp-black.

  PLACEHOLDER ART: flat dark silhouette PNGs (the RM_TwilightSeaFauna.xml
  posture); real art queued to artpipe (twilightsea_<name>_v1).
-->
